OrionLayer open fix 108 — the Space Dragon's bribe on the wire
==============================================================

Work order 319 ("the Space Dragon's bribe", from 316's part E, 315 P7).
orion2re on the fork's branch `orionlayer` (v2.0.0), on top of open fix
107; commit 39c5cc6d. Not on `orionlayer-local`. In src/game/mainpups.cpp
and src/ext/ext_api.cpp under ORION2RE_EXT.

MAINPUPS::Dragon_New_Star_Popup (mainpups.cpp:493; the lines are
the branch's at 21bdc2b8, just before this fix moved them), opened by COMBFIND when the Space
Dragon (attacker 12, NONPLAYER_SHIP_TYPE_DRAGON; the comment there says
"Antarans") reaches a human player's colony (combfind.cpp:157; the
network's :482), ran under the galaxy map's id with nothing on the wire
but its fields. After Update_Dragon_New_Star_Fields (:522) a
TurnPopupGuard reports id 84 and TPOP kind 24 (the kind = id - 60
pairing of 20/80, 22/82, 23/83): args [0] the dragon's star, [1] the
player, [2] COMBFIND::dragon_bribe_bc (capped at 32767), [3] field_mode
(0 the offer, 1 paid: choose a star, 2 too poor — set again after every
input, Evaluate_Dragon_New_Star_Input moves it inside the loop), [4]
mp_fields[2] (refuse / close, ESC), [5] mp_fields[25] (YES, E 561; the
fields are added once, so it stays in modes 1 and 2). The text is the
message as Draw_Dragon_New_Star_Popup last formatted it (E 555, 464 or
583; :2594-2599), copied into a static buffer, the draw's own being a
local. The tail, written on every snapshot: int16 field_mode, int16 n,
n x (int16 star field, int16 star) — the hidden fields
MOVEBOX::Add_Galaxy_Map_Fields_2 added for the popup's galaxy map
(MOX::galaxy_map_star_field); n is NUM_STARS in mode 1, 0 otherwise.
Ended right after the loop, before Do_Popup_Cleanup releases the fields.
Read only.

Live: UNVERIFIED — no live run (Data's decision of 20 October 2026); built
and compiled (`linux-debug`, ORION2RE_EXT on; mainpups.cpp also without
it; a misspelt member refused by the compiler on the scratch clone).

